 (108,'LLM-010','S9 — settle the provider cache-read tokens (cost undercount)','impl','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'specs/llm-full-utilisation.md (S9)','app/Infrastructure/Language/LaravelAiLanguageGateway.php; app/Actions/SettleAiUsageReservationAction.php; app/Models/AiUsageReservation.php; app/Actions/BuildAiPilotReportAction.php; app/Actions/SummarizeAiOperabilityAction.php','DISC-008 output. The SDK Usage exposes cacheReadInputTokens and both parsers subtract it from promptTokens (DeepSeek ParsesTextResponses.php:86; OpenAI :142-148), but LaravelAiLanguageGateway reads promptTokens/completionTokens only and SettleAiUsageReservationAction passes a hardcoded 0 into the cached parameter ResolveAiUsageCostAction already prices. So cached input is invisible: uncounted, never charged at the cached_input rate in config/pricing.php, and no lane reports a cache-hit rate. Carry the value through the existing settle path, store it, count it in the input ceiling (promptTokens + cached), report hits per provider/model. Cache-write tokens stay unplumbed (neither supported provider bills them). Spec: plan/details/specs/llm-full-utilisation.md S9.','2026-09-17 18:11:38'),
 (109,'PVE-001','Campaign momentum: the faction races the same objective (7E instance)','deferred','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'specs/pve-empire.md','app/Models/AiCampaign.php; app/Actions/AdvanceAiCampaignStateAction.php; app/Actions/DeclareAiCampaignObjectiveAction.php','DISC-009 output, research idea 1+2+3 folded. Today an Active campaign resolves only on completion and fails on the deadline; the faction advances nothing, so time is the only opponent. Add one counter on AiCampaign plus the faction''s own declared objective set, advanced by the existing ai:advance-campaigns pass on a published schedule, so the coalition win condition becomes complete the ladder first. Objective ordering (scout -> weaken -> final stronghold) is the escalation ladder and the same counter is the influence bar gating the decisive objective - one number, not two mechanisms. Rewards unchanged (ordinary loot/debris + verified contribution record, paid on completion). Gated by the Package 7 evidence rule: needs a campaign review record naming the gap. Spec: plan/details/specs/pve-empire.md. | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies','2026-09-17 21:13:11'),
 (110,'PVE-002','Coalition campaign page: progress + both sides'' losses (situation log)','deferred','done','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'specs/pve-empire.md','resources/views/; routes/web.php','DISC-009 output, research idea 9. The spec''s deliverable list includes a module-owned coalition-facing campaign page and none exists (only the operator page at admin/ai). Content is decided by the research: objective progress and both sides'' losses as counters aggregated at write time, matching the review loop cheap-to-read rule. Deferred until a disclosed coalition campaign exists - a page for a coalition that does not exist is speculative UI. Spec: plan/details/specs/pve-empire.md. | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies','2026-09-17 21:13:11'),
 (111,'P7-001','7A scope: ordinary-universe consultation (war declaration + new colony triggers)','deferred','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/WORK-PACKAGES.md (Package 7)','app/Actions/RequestCampaignConsultationAction.php; app/Enums/AiCampaignConsultationTrigger.php; app/Actions/BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction.php; config/campaign-consultation.php','Package 7A, audited 17 Sep 2026. The consultation machinery is NOT missing: transport, off/observe/advice admission, staff switch, trigger allowlist, cooldown, concurrency cap, daily ceilings, receipts, deterministic validation, profile-bounded ranking nudge, thinking-model routing and read-only tools all ship (6A/6B/6C + S4/S5/S8). Six triggers already fire: FleetLoss, RepeatedSetback, ContestedObjective, CoalitionConflict, NewPhase, RankChange. What is genuinely left: (a) two unbuilt events - worth adding only when a caller exists: war declaration and new colony; (b) the shipped lane is campaign-keyed - RequestCampaignConsultationAction::handle() takes an AiCampaign and BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction builds from it - so ordinary-universe (non-campaign) advice is a shape change, not a config flag, and needs its own budget, caps and evidence gate. Gate: a review record naming a player-visible gap (Package 7 rule). | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies | blocked: war-declaration trigger has no host seam (grep of host app/ for declare-war/start-war empty); new-colony trigger has no module observation of a colony landing (planned+dispatched only); Package 7 evidence gate needs a review record naming a player-visible gap, which DECISIONS.md records as owner-supplied. Ordinary-universe shape change is dead machinery (gate 2) until a caller exists. | CORRECTED 18 Sep 2026: the colony trigger needs NO host change - the host fires OGame\Events\Game\PlanetCreated (planetId, playerId, planetType) from PlanetServiceFactory:536, and the module already listens to BuildingCompleted (AIServiceProvider:133), so a NewColony listener is module-side only. Only the war trigger lacks a seam (no war feature exists). | UNBLOCKED 18 Sep 2026 for handoff. Colony trigger needs NO host change: the host fires OGame\Events\Game\PlanetCreated(planetId, playerId, planetType) from PlanetServiceFactory:536, and the module already listens to BuildingCompleted (AIServiceProvider:133), so a NewColony listener + a consultation signal are module-side only. Still open: (a) the war trigger has NO host seam (no war feature exists) - either drop it or add the host feature in a paired PR; (b) Package 7''s evidence gate (a review naming a player-visible gap) is owner-supplied. Start with the colony half. | RE-BLOCKED 18 Sep 2026 after RV-011: the colony trigger''s only effect is a consultation signal, but the lane is campaign-keyed (RequestCampaignConsultationAction takes an AiCampaign) and both universes hold 0 campaigns, so a PlanetCreated listener would be dead machinery (gate 2) and untestable. Building it needs an owner decision first: (a) de-campaign the lane into an ordinary-universe shape (own budget/caps/evidence gate), or (b) open a campaign to give the trigger a caller. The war trigger still has no host seam and the Package 7 evidence record is owner-supplied. No deterministic slice is implementable until one of those lands. | DONE 18 Sep 2026 - colony half shipped: AiCampaignConsultationTrigger::NewColony + RecordAiColonyCampaignSignal listener on PlanetCreated (module-side only, no host change), allowlist entry, 5 tests in CampaignColonyTriggerTest, Gate 2 + Pint clean, dev-stack parallel runner green. War-declaration trigger DROPPED: the host has no war-declaration seam, so it would need a paired host PR, not module work. The ordinary-universe de-campaigning shape change stays unbuilt and is tracked as DEF-005 (gate 2: dead machinery until a caller exists).','2026-09-18 14:11:44'),
 (112,'P7-002','7B: semantic recall only if a held-out review beats native retrieval','deferred','done','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/WORK-PACKAGES.md (Package 7)','app/Infrastructure/Memory/AgentOsLongTermMemory.php; app/Domain/Memory/LongTermMemorySelector.php; app/Actions/EvaluateAiSocialExchangeAction.php','Package 7B, audited 17 Sep 2026. Gate: a held-out review showing native retrieval misses what exact/entity recall closes. The starting evidence points the other way. The AgentOS recall benchmark (15 Sep 2026, 30 trials, Modules/AI/scripts/e2e-agentos-recall-benchmark.php, runs inside ogamex-app) measured the driver value as SUBSTITUTION, not addition: the +33.3pp required-fact recall IS the eviction of newest facts (newest-kept 1/30 external vs 30/30 native), with the promotion unbounded, and the sole consumer (NativeSocialCognition::outstandingDebtPenalty) is unreachable in production because every real help request answers Counter: insufficient_available_amount. Reference profile also runs no local model, so any embedder is a paid hosted call. Reopen only with a held-out review that shows a miss native retrieval cannot close. | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies','2026-09-17 22:27:49'),
 (113,'P7-003','7C: PsychSim diplomacy experiment (driver integration + consumer)','deferred','done','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/WORK-PACKAGES.md (Package 7)','','Package 7C, audited 17 Sep 2026. PsychSim appears nowhere in the module (grep of app/, config/, tests/ is empty) and is not one of the four supported drivers (native + FAtiMA/CiF + CBRKit + AgentOS), so this is a driver integration plus a diplomacy consumer - the deepest dependency and the least evidenced of Package 7''s slices. Spec bound: one account and 1-3 relevant counterparts at depth one (depth two needs a recorded measured gain and capacity evidence); it may propose social stance or coalition evidence, never fleets, resources, promises or a replacement player runtime. Gate: Package 6 acceptance + a review record naming the gap. | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies','2026-09-17 21:53:29'),
 (114,'REV-005','Confirm the wave-10 session-cost measurements (W10-1, W10-2)','review','done','P1','W10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/plan/details/GAP-REGISTER.md','Step 0 of the wave-10 performance work, and the reason neither row below may be implemented yet: reproduce the measurements on the committed build before changing code, with the read-only method recorded in the register (a DB::listen listener plus a debug_backtrace walk around one PlayerPerceptionBuilder::build, and the MySQL profiler for the server-side figure). Confirm or correct each figure: 33 queries per GameMissionFactory::getAllMissions() and 0 for the same static metadata read through a class name; ~297 of ~430 perception queries arriving from FacilityChain.php:129; ~34 PlayerService rebuilds per perception from make($id, true) across 20 module and 30 host sites; session jobs 1-36 s while sibling work kinds measure ~310 ms. Deliverable: a note under plan/details/reviews/ with the reproduced figures, the exact call sites, a verdict per row (confirmed / corrected / withdrawn), and for W10-2 the chosen mechanism plus the write-then-reread callers that were audited. No code change in this row. Corrected expectation from the 17 Sep re-measure: the mission path is 105 of 439 perception queries and 4.6-8.0 s of a 19.7-23.1 s build, not 297 queries. Also confirm the environment caveat before trusting any seconds figure: the same statement measures a 45.8 ms median through raw PDO on the application handle and 2.5 ms through the query builder in the same process, so the query counts are the portable finding and the wall clock is a property of this host.','2026-09-17 13:56:15'),
 (115,'IMPL-043','Host mission catalogue without instantiation (W10-1)','impl','done','P1','W10-1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Factories/GameMissionFactory.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php','Only after REV-005 confirms W10-1. GameMission::__construct pulls FleetMissionService and MessageService, and both constructors require a PlayerService, so resolving any mission builds a player: 4 queries for metadata that is already static (getTypeId, getRequiredResearch and getRequiredShipMachineNames are all static methods). Split the id-to-class map out of getAllMissions() into getMissionClasses(): array<int, class-string<GameMission>>; make getAllMissions() map that through resolve() so the callers that genuinely need instances keep working unchanged (FleetController plus the three admin label lists); make getMissionById() look the class up and throw a clear error for an unknown id instead of a match fallthrough. The module side is one line: FacilityChain::missionRequiredResearch() iterates the class list and calls $class::getRequiredResearch(). Acceptance: perception queries ~430 to ~130 measured on the grand universe via a restart, session jobs back in the ~300 ms band, host suite and module suite green, Gate 2 review clean. Correction 17 Sep 2026 after re-measuring: the filed figure was wrong. The catalogue is 105 of 439 perception queries and 4.6-8.0 s of a 19.7-23.1 s build (~24-36%), because the perception reaches it 3 times per build, not 9. So this row is necessary but NOT sufficient - closing it leaves ~15 s, and IMPL-045 (module-side) and IMPL-044 (host) carry the rest. Corrected acceptance: perception queries 439 -> ~334.','2026-09-17 18:11:38'),
 (116,'IMPL-044','One player reload per job (W10-2)','impl','done','P2','W10-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Factories/PlayerServiceFactory.php; app/Services/PlayerService.php','Only after REV-005 confirms W10-2. PlayerServiceFactory::make($id, true) rebuilds a PlayerService on every call (~4 queries each: users, highscores, users_tech, plus PlanetListService planets read) and one perception triggers ~34 rebuilds across 20 module and 30 host forced-reload sites. Smallest mechanism first: memoise a forced reload per generation in PlayerServiceFactory, since AppServiceProvider already flushes the singleton factories before every job (the JobProcessing listener), so a second forced reload inside one job re-reads identical rows. Alternative if the audit finds a write-then-reread caller inside one job: make the PlayerService planet list lazy instead. Risk to settle before choosing, not after: a caller that writes and then relies on a second fresh read in the same job would see stale data. Acceptance: rebuilds per perception ~34 to ~1, perception query count down again, session jobs in the ~300 ms band, host suite and module suite green.','2026-09-17 15:20:42'),
 (117,'IMPL-045','Memoise the mission research map once per worker process (W10-1)','impl','done','P1','W10-1, W10-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Perception/PlayerObservationService.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/','Shipped and deployed 17 Sep 2026: a static memo on FacilityChain, because the host mission catalogue is static and the read was repeated per chain instance (3 catalogue builds per perception). Measured on the grand universe: mission path 105 -> 39 queries, perception 439 -> 372 queries, suite 854/854 green. The player-graph half of the original row was attempted (drop make($id, true) in the 20 read sites) and reverted: it breaks AiCapabilityPublicationTest, because the factory cache is only fresh per job and a host write inside a test/request must still be visible - refiled as IMPL-046.','2026-09-17 13:46:58'),
 (118,'IMPL-046','Resolve the player once per perception instead of per call site (fresh-preserving, W10-2)','impl','done','P2','W10-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/app/Domain/Perception/PlayerObservationService.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/','The remaining module-side half of W10-2, after the naive version was tried and reverted: dropping make($id, true) at the 20 read sites broke AiCapabilityPublicationTest, because the factory cache is only fresh per job and a host write inside a request (or a test) must still be visible. The correct mechanism resolves the PlayerService exactly once per perception - after the session advance has already forced a reload and before any module write - and passes that instance down through PlayerObservationService and into the planners it invokes, so the read path reloads once instead of ~20 times without losing write freshness. Acceptance: the same freshness test stays green, perception queries fall from 372 toward ~300, suite green.','2026-09-17 14:43:48'),
 (119,'IMPL-047','Refuse colonising at the planet cap (live colonise-spam fix)','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/QueueableColonyPlanner.php','Live read 17 Sep (ogamex-grand): the old cohort (players 12-21) dispatched 4,763 colonise missions in 48h, ~2,300 of them cancelled at arrival because every account was at its host-derived planet cap (astrophysics). QueueableColonyPlanner::plan() never checked the cap, so every 5s session re-planned a colony the host would refuse. Fix: refuse in plan() when planets->planetCount() >= getMaxPlanetAmount() (both host answers, gate 1). Verified live: players 12/17/20/26 now return null; ColonySpyExecutorTest 13/13.','2026-09-17 18:21:06'),
 (120,'RV-001','Solar satellite answers an energy shortfall the building queue cannot','impl','done','P2','P3 audit (piecepapercode-barakis)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/EnergyCapacity.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableBuildingPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableUnitPlanner.php','EnergyCapacity::pending() keeps only objects BuildingQueueObject::accepts(), so unit-based energy producers are unreachable and a planet in deficit whose affordable capacity buildings are exhausted falls through while its mines run at a fraction of their output. Run the same cheapest-first scan over the production objects the UNIT queue accepts, published as a unit intent. Seam: ObjectService::getGameObjectsWithProduction() with the unit accepts-check. Accept: frozen-clock case where an exhausted-deficit planet offers a solar-satellite intent while a planet that can still afford a plant offers the plant first; a mod-added energy unit needs no module edit. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:00:15'),
 (121,'RV-002','U6 launch subset: counter-select the launch per target and simulate before dispatch','impl','done','P2','W6-4',NULL,'U5,U6','plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableUnitPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Infrastructure/Battle/NativeRaidEstimator.php','W6-4 shipped only the payload-sized cargo half. Production and launch are two decisions: the stock is what the account owns, the launch is the minimum hulls that win against THIS target. Derive the launch subset from the target-reported hull mix and defence using the host rapid-fire properties, simulate that subset once before dispatch, and let fodder ride only when the target can threaten the heavies. Accept: a light-fighter swarm draws cruisers, the same stock shown an undefended farm sends kill ships plus cargo, and a mod-added rapid-fire pair changes the selection with no module edit. Also the prerequisite for RV-007. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:04:56'),
 (122,'RV-003','Measure the defended-raid loot tier against the host own debris and repair values','review','done','P2','W6-1',NULL,'T7','plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php; Modules/AI/plan/details/reviews/','RaidPlanner::LOOT_TIER_DEFENDED is a fixed 2.0 whose comment says debris subsidises a defended run, while claim RAID-014 decided debris stays out of the single-raid profit gate. One bounded read over existing artifacts (ai_decision_traces score components, ai_action_receipts, the estimator P20 output) asking whether the fixed tier admits a defended run the host debris and defence-repair values do not pay for, and whether it refuses one they do. Deliverable: a dated review record with the before figure and a verdict that either closes this as not-a-defect or points at RV-006. No code change. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:09:25'),
 (123,'RV-004','Mine production percentages as a real lever (throttle under deficit, restore after)','impl','done','P2','P3 audit (ogame-opensource-2-ai)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Actions/SetAiMinePercentAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/EnergyCapacity.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableBuildingPlanner.php','The host lets a planet run each mine at a percentage (planets.*_percent via PlanetService::setBuildingPercent/getBuildingPercent, already exposed to players by ResourcesController) and the module uses neither side. One action and one rule: while the planet is in deficit, lower the mine with the worst output-per-energy to the highest percentage the remaining energy covers; when a capacity building lands, restore it. The object is chosen from host-reported production, never a machine name. Accept: frozen-clock case where exactly one mine is throttled, the host energy balance recovers, a later session restores it, and the receipt records before/after percentages. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:21:47'),
 (124,'RV-005','Confirm an admitted account owns a moon, and record its moon facilities','discovery','done','P3','precondition gate',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md; Modules/AI/plan/details/reviews/','RV-008 and RV-009 cannot start without an owned moon and none exists today: the whole grand universe holds one moon (planets.planet_type = 3) and it is owned outside the cohort. Read planets for planet_type = 3 among admitted accounts, record which account owns one and which moon facilities it has, or record that none exists yet; a moon arrives through ordinary play (host calculateMoonChance on a fleet crash). Accept: a dated line naming the owner and its facilities, or stating none exists. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:12:28'),
 (125,'RV-006','Ground the defended loot tier in the host own debris and repair values','impl','done','P2','W6-1',NULL,'T7','plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php','Closed as not-a-defect: RV-003 measured 1,587 raid receipts (1,033 flown) but zero raid battle-outcome rows, so no debris/repair before-figure exists to contradict the fixed 2.0. Constant kept; reopen with a new row the day defended-raid outcomes are recorded.','2026-09-17 19:11:58'),
 (126,'RV-007','CRN screen-then-confirm ladder across launch subsets','impl','done','P3','P3 audit (peterradzisz-fleet-optimizer)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Infrastructure/Battle/NativeRaidEstimator.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php','One seed stream per candidate so two launch subsets are compared through common random numbers, a cheap screen over all candidates and the wide confirmation spent on the winner. Dead machinery before RV-002, because with fewer than two candidates the ladder has nothing to choose between - that is why it is gated. Accept: two subsets scored through the shared stream rank identically to a single-stream run, and the wide pass runs only on the winner (assert on the sample counter). Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:14:16'),
 (127,'RV-008','Sensor phalanx: build it on an owned moon, then scan the target before the raid','impl','done','P3','P3 audit (alaingilbert-ogame)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueablePhalanxPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/','PhalanxService ships in the host and the module never calls it. A fleeter with a moon scans before committing, and a scan is the only way to see a fleet stationed inside the planet that the espionage report cannot show. The row carries its own prerequisite: build the sensor phalanx on the moon first through the existing building path. Host canScanTarget is the only legality gate and must be respected exactly - an out-of-range scan is a ban risk, not a profit. One candidate source when a phalanx exists and the raid is otherwise viable, folded into the existing observation path. Accept: without a phalanx no scan candidate is published; with one the stationed fleet changes the raid decision; a host-refused scan is recorded and writes no game state. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md | UNBLOCKED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — moon precondition still unmet; gate as recorded. | REALLY UNBLOCKED 17 Sep 2026 — a cohort account now owns moons: user 13 holds moon id 63 (1:8:8) and id 64 (8:365:4), 6 fields each (1 base + 5 class-2 bonus), created through the host''s own PlanetServiceFactory::createMoonForPlanet path. lunar_base canQueue=1; sensor_phalanx and jump_gate become legal once lunar_base 1 stands. Precondition of RV-005 is now satisfied.','2026-09-17 22:15:56'),
 (128,'RV-009','Jump gate: move the fleetsave between own moons instead of flying it','impl','done','P3','P3 audit (janeczkins-xbot)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableFleetSavePlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/QueueAiFleetSaveAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php','JumpGateService ships and is unused. With two owned moons a player moves the parked fleet between them instead of flying it - a save that costs no flight time - and the module fleetsave already ranks own bodies. Add the jump-gate move as one more destination kind the existing ranking can pick when it beats a flight, only when the cooldown and both facilities allow; the row carries building the gate as a FacilityChain step. Low value with a single moon: the mechanism is a destination pair. Accept: with one moon nothing changes; with two, a frozen-clock case picks the jump over the flight and a cooldown-blocked one falls back to the flight. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md | UNBLOCKED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — moon precondition still unmet; gate as recorded. | REALLY UNBLOCKED 17 Sep 2026 — a cohort account now owns moons: user 13 holds moon id 63 (1:8:8) and id 64 (8:365:4), 6 fields each (1 base + 5 class-2 bonus), created through the host''s own PlanetServiceFactory::createMoonForPlanet path. lunar_base canQueue=1; sensor_phalanx and jump_gate become legal once lunar_base 1 stands. Precondition of RV-005 is now satisfied.','2026-09-17 22:24:49'),
 (129,'RV-010','Metal-dump research while the warehouse is full and the planet cannot build','impl','done','P3','P3 audit (trilogi77-ogamebot)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/EconomyUpgrades.php','Trigger measured live 17 Sep: 8 cohort planets metal-capped with idle build/research queues; QueueableBuildingPlanner::plan() returned null for 12/17/18 because those planets are field-full (buildings >= field_max), so every mine is refused by canQueue and the surplus metal was discarded with no sink. spendSurplus() now appends a research dump after the mines: when no mine is queueable the planner falls through to the technology that spends the largest share of its price in the capped resource, host-derived (getResearchObjects + getObjectPrice). Accept: a field-full metal-capped planet plans a research dump (live 12/17/18 -> armor_technology), a planet with free fields keeps mining, a non-capped account is unchanged. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:37:54'),
 (130,'RV-011','Game-phase classification (deferred on a named consumer)','deferred','done','P3','P3 audit (shinigallo-ogame-agi)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/; Modules/AI/plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','TRIGGER: a named consumer that varies a decision on the phase. The audit cut this for having no host seam, but a phase is derivable from host reads (own rank, object levels, the host highscore distribution) with no host change - so the missing piece is a consumer, not a seam. With none it is config for a value nothing varies on (gate 2). Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies | UNBLOCKED 18 Sep 2026 for handoff. Research done - see plan/details/reviews/2026-09-18-rv-011-game-phase-research.md (phase-dependent behaviours, sourced). Recommended consumer: RaidPlanner target-class escalation (inactives early -> actives -> fleet-crashing late). The owner must pick ONE consumer before the classifier is built (gate 2: no config for a value nothing varies on). | IMPLEMENTED 18 Sep 2026 - consumer chosen (autonomous): RaidPlanner target-class escalation. GamePhase enum (early/mid/late) from host reads (astrophysics level, planet count); RaidPlanner::phase() + targetEligible() gate the raid target class (inactives always, actives once colonised, active fleets only at astrophysics 23); inactivity via PlayerService::isInactive() read fresh. Tests: 4 in RaidDepthTest. Gate 2 + Pint clean, module PHPStan no new findings, RaidDepthTest 31 passed.','2026-09-18 13:52:08'),
 (131,'RV-012','Consultation confidence gate and horizon (deferred on the lane and a signal)','deferred','done','P3','P3 audit (shinigallo-ogame-agi)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Actions/BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/ApplyCampaignConsultationRankingAction.php','TRIGGER: the 6A/7A consultation lane enabled AND a confidence source present in the brief. The brief carries no confidence signal today and the lane is off by default, so suppressing a low-confidence nudge has nothing to suppress. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — gate as recorded in the notes above still applies | IN PROGRESS 18 Sep 2026 (owner approved: if the AI advice is not good enough, lean towards the deterministic decision and report it). Working-tree WIP, UNVERIFIED: schema ''confidence'' (0..1) in OgameCampaignConsultationAgent, ai.campaign-consultation.minimum_confidence floor, CampaignConsultationRecommendation::mayMoveRanking() gate in ApplyCampaignConsultationRankingAction, AiStopReason::ConsultationLowConfidence reported from ConsultCampaignDecisionAction. NEXT: run the consultation suites + bash scripts/ogamex gate, then mark done. Tests updated: CampaignConsultationRankingTest, CampaignConsultationWiringTest, CampaignConsultationGatewayTest.','2026-09-18 13:07:33'),
 (132,'RV-013','Moonshot: sacrificial self-battle to farm debris (cut, not deferred)','deferred','deferred','P3','P3 audit (trilogi77-ogamebot)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','CUT, recorded so it is not re-mined. AttackMission::checkOwnPlanet refuses self-attacks by design, so the self-battle seam does not exist; and sending a fleet to die on a neighbour to farm the debris is machine-shaped against gate 3 - no ordinary player does it. Reopens only if the owner asks for the host seam and a named-play justification. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md | UN-DEFERRED (owner direction, 17 Sep 2026) — still CUT (host self-battle seam absent); un-deferred for visibility only | CLOSED 18 Sep 2026 (owner): real players do not do this, so the AI will not either.','2026-09-18 04:50:31'),
 (133,'W11-1','Ferry quote spent before dispatch — the transfer loop was refused by the host','impl','done','P1','W11-1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/QueueAiTransferAction.php; app/Domain/Decision/QueueableTransferPlanner.php; app/Enums/AiQueueActionReason.php','Closed 17 Sep 2026. Clamp the shipment to the source''s stock at dispatch, abandon a remnant below MINIMUM_SHIPMENT as source_short_at_dispatch, leave FleetMissionService::calculateConsumption fuel behind. Measured: 617/618 transfers refused in an hour before; 0 host resource refusals and 13 flown in the 90s after. 867 module tests green.','2026-09-17 18:38:02'),
 (134,'IMPL-048','Refuse planning a ferry the source cannot carry (live no_transport_fleet churn)','impl','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/QueueableTransferPlanner.php; tests/Feature/TransferDepthTest.php','Live read 18 Sep (ogamex-grand, 2h window): 274 no_transport_fleet refusals, the largest refusal class — a surplus ferry planned from a near-cap colony owning no cargo ships, re-planned every session. QueueableTransferPlanner now gates both source passes on the host''s getTotalCargoCapacity > 0 before publishing, so an unflyable ferry is never planned; the dispatch refusal stays as the safety net for cargo that leaves between plan and dispatch. 5 tests updated in TransferDepthTest.','2026-09-17 22:41:41'),
 (135,'IMPL-049','Campaign objective resolution must ignore non-Active campaigns','impl','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/ResolveAiCampaignObjectiveFromBattleReportAction.php','Live evidence 18 Sep (ogamex-pve): campaign 1 reached FactionWon at 13:47, yet a battle report at objective planet 2 at 14:03 still recorded consultation signal 4 (contested_objective) against it. The action selects objectives by planet_id and completed_at IS NULL only, with no join to the campaign state, so a FactionWon, Resolved or Failed campaign keeps producing signals. ConsultCampaignDecisionAction only ever consumes signals belonging to the Active campaign, so those rows can never be consumed and accumulate permanently. The same missing filter also lets an attacker victory mark an objective complete inside a dead campaign. Fix: restrict both the completed_at update and the contested signal to objectives whose campaign state is Active. Proof: a Pest test that a battle at an objective planet of a FactionWon campaign writes no signal and completes nothing.','2026-09-18 14:27:31'),
 (136,'IMPL-050','Pace faction campaign momentum by the window, not by the pass','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/AdvanceAiCampaignStateAction.php','Live evidence 18 Sep (ogamex-pve): campaign 1 opened with 3 objectives at 13:41 and reached FactionWon at 13:47, five minutes into a seven-day window. Momentum advances one rung per ai:advance-campaigns pass and the scheduler runs that pass every minute, so a campaign ends after N minutes where N is the number of declared strongholds. Campaign 2 with 6 objectives climbed to momentum 6 of 6 the same way. The action already carries a ponytail note naming this ceiling. Fix: derive the rung from elapsed time in the window, for example floor(elapsed / window * objective count), so the ladder cannot outrun the published schedule, keeping the counter as the single influence bar the campaign page reads. Proof: a frozen-clock test asserting a seven-day campaign with three objectives is still Active after an hour and reaches FactionWon only near the deadline.','2026-09-18 14:25:36'),
 (137,'DISC-010','FleetSave and Recall are unobservable at 1000x fleet speed','discovery','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Perception/PlayerObservationService.php','Measured 18 Sep. FleetSave was offered 4 times in 58448 grand traces and 0 in 12713 pve traces; Recall 4 in 58448. The planner itself is healthy: run directly against 8 live grand accounts it returned a save for every one, with fleet values from 12.6M to 127.5M against exposure bands of 5k to 50k. The reactive candidate requires currentPlayerUnderAttack() plus a non-espionage inbound, and at fleet_speed 1000 an attack averages 5.7s with 0 missions in flight whenever sampled, so the window is almost never observed. The proactive path needs an absence above PROACTIVE_SAVE_MIN_ABSENCE_MINUTES while the harness session interval is seconds. Consequence: the accelerated cohorts cannot validate save behaviour, so the goal metric of whether a save ever fails is unmeasurable there. Decide between measuring saves in a 1x universe and recording the limit as permanent. Proof: one 1x round with an observed inbound and a save that fails.','2026-09-18 14:35:47'),
 (138,'DISC-011','Coalition-side campaign triggers need a non-faction account','discovery','done','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'All four coalition triggers are produced only by battles involving a non-faction player: FleetLoss and RepeatedSetback need a faction side wiped by a non-faction attacker, ContestedObjective needs a committed coalition battle at a stronghold, and CoalitionConflict needs two non-faction players fighting. ogamex-pve holds 20 users of which 19 are enabled AiProfile rows, so exactly one non-faction account exists, and 454 battle reports produced no fleet-loss signal. In practice only new_phase and rank_change fire live, which is what the 18 Sep run observed. Decide whether the campaign needs a seeded human-side account, opponent AI actors, or acceptance that four of six triggers stay dormant until the disclosed coalition exists.','2026-09-18 14:35:47'),
 (139,'DISC-012','Alliance life cannot bootstrap in a universe with no alliances','discovery','done','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/AdvanceAllianceLifeAction.php','Live evidence 18 Sep (ogamex-pve): ai:advance-alliance-life reported Applied 0 accounts while alliances and alliance_members were both 0. The action applies an enabled profile to the alliance its tier would join, so with no alliance in existence no account can ever join one and the capability stays unreachable until a human creates the first alliance. Decide whether the faction should found the first alliance or whether this stays human-seeded, and record the answer so the capability is not read as shipped-but-silent.','2026-09-18 14:35:04'),
 (140,'REV-006','Consultation rejection rate from evidence-citation fabrication','review','done','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Live run 18 Sep produced 3 consultation receipts against deepseek-flash: player 10 new_phase invalid (1034/461 tokens), player 16 new_phase completed with a null candidate, player 6 contested_objective completed with candidate 5, every one changed_ranking 0 under observe. The brief carries no evidence at all because ConsultCampaignDecisionAction calls the lane without the evidence argument, so evidenceIds is always empty, while the agent instructions ask the model to cite only supplied evidence ids. A direct reproduction returned evidence_ids of 1 and 2 against a brief carrying no evidence, which the validator rejects as citesUnknownEvidence and discards the whole recommendation. Decide between telling the model that no evidence exists, supplying real driver evidence, or treating an empty supplied list as satisfied. Proof: a frozen brief fixture asserting the intended behaviour plus a measured acceptance rate over N real calls.','2026-09-18 14:31:03'),
 (141,'DEF-005','Ordinary-universe consultation: de-campaign the lane for non-campaign advice','deferred','deferred','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/app/Actions/RequestCampaignConsultationAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction.php','Follow-up from P7-001. The consultation lane is campaign-keyed (RequestCampaignConsultationAction takes an AiCampaign and BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction builds from it), so ordinary-universe (non-campaign) advice is a shape change needing its own budget, caps and evidence gate, not a config flag. TRIGGER: a named ordinary-universe caller plus an owner decision on scope and budgets. The war-declaration trigger additionally needs a host seam that does not exist today (no war feature in the host).','2026-09-18 14:11:44'),
 (142,'IMPL-051','Owner console: render the pilot window on admin/ai','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-1. Add a days=1|7|30 window selector (fixed allow-list, default 1) and a section rendering BuildAiPilotReportAction->handle(days)->toArray() on the existing admin/ai page. Reuse AiPilotReport; do not recompute. Show the report''s own readCost. Test: page figures equal toArray() field by field; out-of-list days falls back to 1.','2026-09-18 15:45:30'),
 (143,'IMPL-052','Owner console: authenticity panel','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-2. Four derived figures: reaction delay (ai_observations.observed_at -> first ai_decision_traces.created_at, vs the 120-180s window PlayerObservationService plans), save outcomes from ai_action_receipts (show refusals/losses, never a success rate), growth curve via AiScoreReport, breadth (distinct decision reasons + distinct contacted accounts). Reuse IMPL-051''s window selector. Test: two seeded accounts (in-window + varied vs late + single action) separate on all four.','2026-09-20 09:42:32'),
 (144,'IMPL-053','Owner console: unified per-account progress board','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-3. No unified per-account view exists today - every reading is a count or a cohort aggregate. score() in BuildAiPilotReportAction already groups by player_id, computes each delta, then keeps only min/median/max/zero-count: keep the per-account deltas in AiScoreReport (one field) and render one row per enabled profile (identity, state now, window progress, last action+outcome, alerts), sorted alert-first then staleness, each row linking to GET admin/ai/account/{player} (named ai.account) built on ExplainAiDecisionAction::forPlayer(). Do NOT derive growth in the page - that would be a second implementation of the growth rule. Test: three accounts (growing/varied, flat, silent) all listed with real deltas, flat+silent ordered above growing, account page shows only that account''s traces. Also: per-row ''view as'' posting the account username to the HOST''s existing admin/developer-shortcuts/impersonate route (lab404/laravel-impersonate; canBeImpersonated()=true for every user, so AI accounts are included). No new controller, session handling or permission check - the host''s admin group and admin-menu leave-link already cover it. Label it for inspection: a human acting while the scheduler drives the same account is two writers and the human holds no lease, so name the population switch as the way to stop new work first. Post to the HOST route - do not call app(''impersonate''): the module declares no runtime dependency on lab404/laravel-impersonate and its vendor tree lacks it, so a class import would be a phantom dependency. take() quietLogins the target, so Auth::user() becomes the AI account and the module''s admin-gated console is unreachable until the host''s leave link is used - one-way by design, the host menu is the way back.','2026-09-20 09:42:32'),
 (147,'IMPL-054','Owner console: liveness and quiet diagnosis','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-4. Answer ''quiet because the game is quiet, or because we are broken''. Three existing figures: newest ai_schedules.last_activity_at (when anything last ran), count of accounts past next_due_at by more than one interval, and the queued/leased work-item counts SummarizeAiOperabilityAction already computes. Link to Horizon for the worker side - do not rebuild queue monitoring. Test: one account due in the past with no activity + one future-dated with recent activity reports one overdue and a fresh last run; all-future reports quiet-but-healthy.','2026-09-20 09:05:35'),
 (148,'IMPL-055','Owner console: storage and retention health','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-5. ai:prune runs daily 03:30 and prints its count to stdout where it is lost; a silently stalled prune is a disk outage on the 2GB profile. Show bounded row counts plus, per windowed table, the oldest row''s age against that table''s own declared retention window - retention that stopped keeping up announces itself, so persist NO prune counter (a second source of truth for the same fact). ai_score_samples is kept for months, so read it against its own window. Test: an in-window row plus an older-than-window row reports the table behind; in-window-only reports healthy.','2026-09-20 09:05:35'),
 (149,'IMPL-056','Owner console: provider visibility per vendor','impl','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-6. Plan-committed: R2-R5 lists ''operator visibility'' as remaining. Per vendor and per day: attempts, outcomes, latency, tokens incl. cached input, cost from ai_language_requests + ai_usage_reservations (both already store provider/model/latency/tokens/cost); consultation receipts carry the same fields. Never per account - the vendor is a lane, not a persona. With both gateways Null, report ''no provider configured'' rather than a table of zeroes. Lower urgency while the paid lanes are off for the peak. Test: seeded requests across two vendors report per-vendor figures with no per-account rows; empty ledger reports the unconfigured state.','2026-09-20 09:05:35'),
 (150,'IMPL-057','Owner console: stop one account','impl','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/owner-ui.md','OW-7. The switch stops the whole population; an owner with one misbehaving account has no smaller move. ai_profiles.enabled already exists and is already read by admission (ResolveAiAdmissionAction) and the social/campaign gates - one form on the board row plus a reason recorded the way the universe switch records who/why/when. A flag, not a delete: a stopped account keeps memory, relationships and obligations. State the caveat on the control: stopping silences the account (no replies, no campaign contribution) - a stop, not a pause. Test: stopping one of three takes no new work for it while the other two continue; resume returns it; reason+actor recorded.','2026-09-20 09:05:35'),
 (152,'DEF-006','AI alliance leader reviews and decides applications','impl','done','P2',NULL,'G18,S1,S2',NULL,'plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','app/Actions/ReviewAiAllianceApplicationsAction.php; app/Domain/Social/ApplicationDecision.php; config/alliance.php; app/Actions/AdvanceAiAllianceLifeAction.php; tests/Feature/AllianceApplicationReviewTest.php','Leader half of alliance life (DEF-003 shipped only the join half). Accept/decline pending applications by tier fit (rank-ratio mirror of AllianceChoice), hard-decline floor fails, at most 1-2 per pass after a minimum age, deterministic, via host acceptApplication/rejectApplication as founder. Gate 3: tier-selective leader through a rank-gated button; gate 1: host data only; gate 2: one action one sort key. Spec: plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','2026-09-19 22:49:47'),
 (153,'DEF-007','Leader welcomes an accepted member','impl','done','P3',NULL,'G18,S1',NULL,'plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','app/Actions/QueueAiAuthoredReplyAction.php; tests/Feature/AllianceApplicationReviewTest.php','On accept, send one short authored welcome via DeliverAiDirectReplyAction; host already assigns the newcomer rank. Gate 3: a leader communicates with a new member; gate 2: reuse the authored pipeline. Spec: plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','2026-09-19 22:49:47'),
 (154,'DEF-008','Observe and answer alliance chat','impl','done','P2',NULL,'S1,G18',NULL,'plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','app/Actions/RecordObservedChatMessageAction.php; app/Actions/RunAiConversationCycleAction.php; app/Actions/DeliverAiDirectReplyAction.php','SHIPPED — false re-open (stale 15-Sep register). Alliance chat is observed and answered: RecordObservedChatMessageAction::handleAlliance + RunAiConversationCycleAction::answerAlliance + DeliverAiAllianceReplyAction. Proof: AllianceChatLifeTest (4 tests). Live 0 because no AI has SENT alliance chat yet — that is DEF-018 (speak first), not this task.','2026-09-21 11:09:29'),
 (155,'DEF-009','Accept buddy requests from existing contacts','impl','done','P3',NULL,'S3',NULL,'plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','app/Actions/ReviewAiBuddyRequestsAction.php; app/Providers/AIServiceProvider.php; tests/Feature/BuddyRequestReviewTest.php','Accept buddy requests from existing contacts only (S3), via host BuddyService. Gate 3: accept from someone you know; gate 1: contact from relationship/exchange records. Spec: plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','2026-09-19 22:49:47'),
 (156,'DEF-010','Observe an ally under attack (ACS-defend trigger)','impl','done','P3',NULL,'G18,ACS',NULL,'plan/details/specs/alliance-social-completion.md','app/Actions/RecordObservedBattleReportAction.php; app/Observers/ObserveCommittedBattleReport.php','SHIPPED — RecordObservedBattleReportAction::recordAllyUnderAttackObservations observes a committed attack on a co-member. Proof: AllyUnderAttackObservationTest (2 tests).','2026-09-21 11:09:29'),
 (157,'DEF-011','A losing battle scars the relationship and is remembered','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/AppraiseObservedBattleReportAction.php','see plan/details/specs/relational-memory.md','2026-09-20 07:52:44'),
