 (339,'DEF-001','Ceiling the standing wall so its size follows the threat, not the exposure clock','deferred','todo','P1','WALL_CEILING',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Domain/Decision/DefenseNeedEvaluator.php','Evidence: QUALITY invariant WALL_CEILING in scripts/verify-cohorts.php fires on 20+ planets; scripts/probe-planet-choice.php prints the per-planet need. DECIDED 30 Sep 2026 (judge): size the standing wall from a modelled attacker''s raiding fleet, not from exposure, and cap the total one planet may hold. That is what an ordinary player does and it needs no constant the owner has to bless; a blanket per-planet ceiling is the fallback only if the modelled number cannot be derived from host data. Overrule by editing this line.

Un-deferred 30 Sep 2026 on the owner directive that defence must be taken care of: the ceiling is not a nicety. 60+ planets sit above it, worst 1,285,633 units on one planet, and the exposure-sized target is what drove 50.8M paid, unbuilt defence units onto grand and 101.8M onto pve.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (340,'DEF-002','State an alliance fit rule so the cohort does not converge on one club','deferred','todo','P1','ALLIANCE_SHARE',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Domain/Social/AllianceChoice.php','Evidence: QUALITY invariant ALLIANCE_SHARE in scripts/verify-cohorts.php. DECIDED 30 Sep 2026 (judge): the fit criterion is language plus activity band (both readable from host state), and founders are chosen per archetype so no single club absorbs the cohort. No member ceiling: it is the least player-authentic of the three. Overrule by editing this line.

Un-deferred 30 Sep 2026: the alliance lane is static (0 applications in 7 days, one alliance holding 75% of the cohort), so the fit rule is now load-bearing rather than theoretical.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (341,'DEF-003','Treat the cohort quality verdict as part of a slice''s acceptance','review','todo','P2','The three verification layers (reachability, scenario expect, canary liveness) prove the accounts PLAY, not that they play WELL: every one of them passed while the cohort walled one planet and left 125 naked. A slice can be fully green and still make play worse.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The quality verdict now exists: scripts/verify-cohorts.php prints QUALITY: PASS/FAIL with three measured invariants (naked-beside-walled, wall ceiling, alliance share) and scripts/harness-live.sh blares QUALITY FAILED each pass. What is missing is the reviewer step: ai-change-review must read the newest verdict and refuse a slice whose behaviour it fails, or say why the invariant is wrong.','2026-09-29 10:26:04'),
 (342,'FOR-013','Section 4 shows the module has no opinion on colony placement, so add a data-driven placement policy: adjacent…','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'resources/behavior/colony.yaml (new) app/Ai/Colony/ColonyPlacementPolicy.php (new) tests/Feature/ColonyPlacementPolicyTest.php (new)','auto-promoted from plan/research/ogame/proposals/FOR-013.md; UNREVIEWED — the plan is deterministically validated but no human has agreed to it yet. Approach by variant: none (facts only) | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
