! [NAKED_BESIDE_WALLED] player 17: 7 planet(s) at zero defence while one holds 39,173 units','2026-09-29 12:36:28'),
 (346,'REV-8','Owner decision: adopt hosted classification (TypeSafe Jev) and provision the key','review','blocked','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-decision-model.md, plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md, plan/details/specs/budgets.md',NULL,'Blocked on the owner, nothing in the JEV-* family starts before this. Needs: (1) approval of paid hosted classification for the language/social lanes, with budgets.md''s ''0 generative calls'' ordinary-gameplay rule amended for that named lane; (2) TYPESAFE_API_KEY in the host .env plus a typesafe provider entry in the host config/ai.php; (3) confirmation of the model pin jev-1.13.0 rather than jev-latest, and a monthly sub-budget inside the existing ai.cognition.monthly_cost_usd wall. The credential is needed at JEV-1 only, which runs over raw HTTP and needs no SDK change. Read plan/details/research/jev-decision-model.md and jev-opportunity-map.md. | blocked: owner decision plus TYPESAFE_API_KEY provisioning and the budgets.md amendment; see notes','2026-09-30 10:28:35'),
 (347,'IMPL-65','Laravel AI SDK ^1.0 upgrade (usage rename + backfill migration)','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/laravel-ai-sdk.md','app/Infrastructure/Language/LaravelAiLanguageGateway.php','The host composer.json pins laravel/ai ^0.11 and the installed copy is v0.11.2. v1.0 renames the usage object promptTokens/completionTokens to inputTokens/outputTokens, and LaravelAiLanguageGateway reads the old names, so the bump is not free. Bump in the HOST composer.json, publish and run the v1.0 backfill migration (conversation storage - we do not use the SDK conversation store, so most of the breakage list does not touch us), keep LaravelAiLanguageTest and LaravelAiHttpFixtureTest green, and prove provider-off behaviour is unchanged. Add no new capability in this slice. Jev-enabling but justified on its own: a first-party package on 0.x beta. See plan/details/specs/laravel-ai-sdk.md. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (348,'DEF-33','One attack cap is stated three times with two values','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/repos/half-wired-play-loops.md, plan/details/specs/gameplay-algorithms.md','app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php','RaidPlanner::BASHING_LIMIT = 6, RaidWavePlan::WAVE_LIMIT = 6 and DailyAttackBudget::MAX_ATTACKS_PER_TARGET_PER_DAY = 8 - one of the three is wrong. half-wired-play-loops.md also records that the host never reports the bashing limit (FleetController only ever returns false), so a universe that tunes it diverges, which is a gate 1 concern. Pick one source of truth: read a host surface if one exposes the limit, else keep one constant with its source named, and make the other two reference it. Add the test that fails today. | UPDATE 30 Sep 2026: DailyAttackBudget is now orphaned — its only caller, app/Ai/Planner/AttackPlanner.php, was deleted with the unreferenced app/Ai/** tree in e23db11. So resolving this is partly a deletion decision: keep RaidPlanner::BASHING_LIMIT as the single source of truth and drop the orphan (QUAL-5), or wire the budget object and make it read the same constant. Either way one value, stated once, with its source named.','2026-09-30 12:12:57'),
 (349,'DEF-34','aid and threat have no consumer, so Gratitude and Fear are unreachable','impl','deferred','P2','W7-2',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-with-cognition-drivers.md, plan/details/specs/external-drivers.md','app/Actions/MapObservedBattleReportToStimulusAction.php','The stimulus hard-codes ''aid'' => 0.0 and ''threat'' => 0.0, so on the only wired appraisal path neither aid > harm nor threat > harm can ever hold and only Anger is reachable from NativeAffectEngine and FatimaAffectEngine. The docblock says threat needs the follow-up signals the experience extractor owns. Name the consumer BEFORE adding any signal (gate 2): which observations produce aid evidence (ally defence, transfer received, warning given) and where the value reaches affect. Blocks JEV-6. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (350,'DEF-35','Hardcoded admin username stands in for a host authority','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','app/Domain/Decision/QueueableSpyPlanner.php','Line 187: if (?->getUsername(false) === ''Legor'') { continue; } stands in for the protected administrator (user 1 is the seeded out-of-cohort admin planet, see specs/reopened-repo-value.md). Use the host''s own signal - PlayerObservationService already reads isAdmin(), isBanned() and isInVacationMode() - so the rule survives any universe and any operator rename. Add a test.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (351,'DEF-36','Two DefenseCompositionPlanner classes and three dome-name spellings','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md, plan/details/specs/external-drivers.md','app/Domain/Decision/DefenseCompositionPlanner.php','The duplicate is resolved: commit e23db11 deleted app/Ai/Defense/DefenseCompositionPlanner.php (the fodder-ratio twin) with the unreferenced app/Ai/** tree, the pipeline now refuses a duplicate class name, and Domain/Decision/DefenseCompositionPlanner (doctrine over YAML) is the only planner. What remains is (a) one unit named two ways across the data — small_shield_dome in resources/behavior/defence-fodder-heavy.yaml and the doctrine constant, SmallShieldDome in resources/scenarios/*.json — so nothing tests that they agree, and (b) confirming app/Ai/Defense/FodderHeavyDefenseDoctrine still has a consumer now that its planner is gone. Normalise the spellings through the host object registry (gate 1) and add one test that the behaviour data, the scenarios and the host agree on every unit name.','2026-09-30 12:12:57'),
 (352,'DEF-37','Doctrine stop_rule is prose parsed by regex, and rewordings fail silently','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md, resources/behavior/defence-doctrines.yaml','app/Domain/Decision/DefenseCompositionPlanner.php','afterStopRule() matches /swap to ([a-z_]+) once the wall passes (\d+)/ against the doctrine sentence ''swap to big_gun_heavy once the wall passes 200 Light Lasers'', and the file''s own comment says rewording the sentence silently disables the handover. Make it structured data (stop_rule as doctrine plus after: unit and count) and keep the verbatim source line beside it as the quote. Add a test that a rewording cannot silently change which doctrine is chosen. Do NOT solve this with a model - see jev-opportunity-map.md section 2.6.','2026-09-30 10:28:35'),
 (353,'DEF-38','Wire or drop the minimum_deterrent floor','impl','todo','P2','W7-1',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md, resources/behavior/defence-doctrines.yaml','app/Domain/Decision/DefenseNeedEvaluator.php','defence-doctrines.yaml carries minimum_deterrent: 4000 (sourced GF-007) with ''NOT READ BY CODE YET: the evaluator still derives need from exposure alone''. Either consume it in DefenseNeedEvaluator or record why it is dropped. RE-CHECK the current contents first - this file and AiDefenseDoctrine were edited recently. Note the doctrine file''s rationale, stated_ceiling, known_weakness and constraints blocks are read by nothing either; if the floor lands, the doctrine''s own reasons are the next candidate.','2026-09-30 11:02:49'),
 (354,'QUAL-4','Quality gate: a class with no production consumer must fail','impl','done','P1','W7-3',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/overengineering-gate.md, plan/details/research/repos/half-wired-play-loops.md','scripts/strategy-pipeline.py','The sweep found roughly 18 classes referenced by nothing outside their own file and their own test - WaveFarmPlanner, PillageCap, NapPolicy, DefMinerStance, IonCannonShieldFodder, Ai/Defence/QueueableDefencePlanner, DailyAttackBudget, AttackPlanner and others - several of them generated by this pipeline (evidence in plan/research/ogame/attempts/WIK-*.log, catalogued in plan/details/research/repos/half-wired-play-loops.md). Add a gate 2 finding for a new class with no production consumer, using cheap reference counting in the gate/quality path, so the next generated slice is either wired or deleted. Also include written-but-unread values of the same family (ai_memory_facts.expires_at never set, AiMemoryPredicate::AttackReceived written and never queried). Do not delete the existing ones in this task - report them first. | DONE 30 Sep 2026 by the harness commit e23db11: strategy-pipeline gained unavailable_files() (a file the attempt created is not its own runtime caller — "nothing calls X, not a delivery, restored") and refuses a class name the module already declares (strategy-pipeline.py:490). The unreferenced app/Ai/** tree including the second DefenseCompositionPlanner was deleted with the 25 test files that were its only caller. Survivors of the same shape are QUAL-5.','2026-09-30 12:12:57'),
 (355,'DOC-7','Record the classification (Jev) activation gate in the plan','doc','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/phase-3-cognition.md, plan/details/specs/budgets.md','plan/details/specs/phase-3-cognition.md','Add hosted classification to the later-capabilities and activation-gates table: the trigger (a measured reading gap on a named lane), the measurement bar (offline agreement, coverage, and confidence-versus-correctness on recorded rows), its own reservation lane and sub-budget, the provider-off guarantee, and the privacy line that chat text leaves the host only on an approved lane. Add one line to budgets.md for the ordinary-path paid-call question, and link the three research notes (jev-decision-model.md, jev-with-cognition-drivers.md, jev-opportunity-map.md). | done 30 Sep 2026 with the plan edits: activation gate row in phase-3-cognition.md, model-call-policy bullet in budgets.md, the hosted-classification spec, and pointers from README, WORK-PACKAGES, external-drivers and GAP-REGISTER (wave 7).','2026-09-30 11:02:49'),
 (356,'JEV-1','Offline reading run: does Jev beat the rules where it matters?','discovery','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-decision-model.md, plan/details/research/jev-with-cognition-drivers.md, plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md','scripts/jev-reading-benchmark.py','Raw POST /v1/systemone from Python - no SDK change needed, so this is the cheapest possible first experiment and the only JEV task the credential directly enables. Replay recorded rows (ai_social_exchanges, host ChatMessage, ai_observations) and compare against the incumbent rules: (a) which exchange is this message, versus ClassifyInboundSocialExchangeAction''s cascade AND its nulls; (b) is this message coercive, versus the AiSocialTerm::Coercive regex; (c) does this apology name the harm, versus the harm-word test; (d) NEW - does this message declare absence or availability (''gn, cya tomorrow''), which has no incumbent at all. Print agreement, a redacted disagreement list with raw quotes, coverage gain on the nulls, confidence-versus-correctness, p50/p95 latency and settled cost. Pass bar: confidence must separate right from wrong on our own data, disagreement must be defensible to a human reading the raw message, and coverage gain must be worth the spend. Refuse to run without the key; require --confirm for real rows. Costed at roughly 0.002 cents per message in jev-decision-model.md. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (357,'JEV-2','ClassificationGateway seam (null plus Laravel AI), off by default','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/laravel-ai-sdk.md, plan/details/research/jev-decision-model.md','app/Contracts/ClassificationGateway.php','Mirror the language lane exactly: a ClassificationGateway contract, a NullClassificationGateway that returns a typed disabled result without touching provider config, and a Laravel-AI-backed implementation that builds the state, maps typed answers into module types, and classifies transport versus schema failure. Bind in AIServiceProvider. Add the ai-settings.yaml and config/cognition.php classification block (enabled false, pinned jev-1.13.0 rather than jev-latest, timeout, state character cap, per-universe/player daily limits, thresholds per question) and one config/pricing.php row for typesafe.jev-1.13.0 with input 0.042 and output 0. Reserve before dispatch and settle once through the existing ledger; store the raw probability beside the derived boolean so a threshold change can be replayed. One seam, three files - no registry, no per-lane gateway. See jev-with-cognition-drivers.md section 6. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (358,'JEV-3','Inbound exchange classification as a fallback cascade','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-with-cognition-drivers.md','app/Actions/ClassifyInboundSocialExchangeAction.php','Only when the regex cascade returns null: one Choice over the known AiSocialExchangeType cases plus an explicit other, with authored criteria, one Boolean for whether the message names terms, and a confidence threshold. The resource and amount stay parsed by the existing regex, and RecordAiLanguageProposalAction::termsAreExplicit() keeps re-checking any proposal against the raw message, so a model answer can never invent a resource or an amount. Low confidence is today''s silence; provider-off or budget-exhausted is today''s silence. The deterministic path stays the fast path and the floor. See jev-with-cognition-drivers.md section 5I. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (359,'JEV-4','Read availability and absence declarations from chat','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md','app/Domain/Perception/ActivityIntelReader.php','Nothing in the module models when a target sleeps - the sweep answered ''not found'', the only uptime statement is the 15-minute star and exp(-minutes/15). Players announce absence in chat and the module already reads every inbound message with a matcher that forgets anything it cannot transact. Add a bounded read (one Boolean plus one Choice over authored horizons) and store it as an expiring fact - ai_memory_facts.expires_at exists and is never set today - for raid timing to read. Must not gate a raid on a provider call, must store the raw probability, and must be deduped per message. Authenticity: this is what a human does, ''he said he is off to bed, launch now''. This is the most novel idea in jev-opportunity-map.md section 2.3 and needs the owner''s explicit nod in REV-8 because it is a new behavioural input. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (360,'JEV-5','Read alliance pitch and application quality instead of testing for non-empty text','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md','app/Domain/Social/AllianceChoice.php','AllianceChoice.php line 92:  = trim(external_text . application_text) !== '''' ? 1.0 : 0.0, worth half a quality point beside  * 2.0, so ''did anyone type anything'' scores a decision an account lives with. ReviewAiAllianceApplicationsAction reads no application text at all - rank ratio and age only - although the pitch term''s own comment says a readable pitch is the applicant''s own filter. Replace the non-empty test with one bounded read at decision time (once per account or per application, so the cost is negligible) and read the application text in the review action IF the host exposes it - verify that column before relying on it. If either lane is refused, delete the term rather than scoring a non-empty string 1.0 (gate 2). | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (361,'JEV-6','Appraisal variables for the affect driver','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-with-cognition-drivers.md','app/Infrastructure/Cognition/FatimaAffectEngine.php','FatimaAffectEngine::branch() pre-selects the OCC action and signs desirability and threat from three numbers, while the stimulus hard-codes aid and threat at 0.0 with an ownShare of 0.5 as the cutoff. One request, several questions (desirability as a Score, deliberateness, can-strike-again, received-help) over a bounded state; the module maps the answers onto the signed OCC beliefs and FAtiMA keeps computing emotion intensity and mood. Never let the model pick the emotion label or fill mood, driverEmotion or driverIntensity - those are the driver''s mechanism. Blocked by DEF-34 because aid and threat have no consumer today, and a model question without a consumer is a gate 2 failure. See jev-with-cognition-drivers.md section 5A. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (362,'JEV-7','Harness provenance check: does the cited source support this constant?','impl','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/jev-opportunity-map.md, plan/details/research/strategy-principles.md','scripts/strategy-pipeline.py','One question per authored constant in resources/behavior and the corpus: does the cited source support this value, and is the claim DOCUMENTED, CONTESTED or STRATEGIC_HEURISTIC (the vocabulary the corpus already uses). This guards the rule the research pipeline exists to protect - every behaviour value must resolve to a source id and nothing is authored. Output is a reviewable report; it never edits resources/behavior and never becomes a value. Runs at authoring and review time only, never inside an account. This is the citation-check shape TypeSafe documents, and the cheapest Jev win in the set because a wrong answer costs nothing. | PRIORITY (owner, 30 Sep 2026): hosted classification runs after the strategy workstream is completely finished; see REV-9, which every JEV task and IMPL-65 now depends on. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (363,'DEF-39','Human-behaviour constants live in an enum instead of resources/behavior','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Enums/AiSkillBand.php','The module instruction says human-behaviour constants belong in resources/behavior. AiSkillBand carries variationWeight 8/4/1, selectionMargin 10/2.5/1, evidenceReaction 1.0/0.5/0.2 and idleOverrideProbability 0.05/0.02/0.01 in PHP, and its own comment calls them ''three unmeasured rates''. Move them into a behaviour resource (or record why they stay in code) so a skill band can be retuned without a code edit and the tuned values are reviewable beside the rest of the behaviour data. Gate 2: if the resource would hold nothing else, record the decision rather than building a loader.','2026-09-30 11:02:48'),
 (364,'DISC-13','Calibration loop for the decision weights (measure, do not model)','discovery','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/UtilityScorer.php','The decision engine''s weights are hand-picked (UtilityScorer RESOURCE_NEED_WEIGHT 30, SAFETY_WEIGHT 50, TARGET_CONFIDENCE_WEIGHT 30, TRAVEL_COST_WEIGHT 25, RECOVERY_WEIGHT 20, ARCHETYPE_WEIGHT 25; CandidateActionFactory::features() taste table; archetype preferences; SURVIVAL_FLOOR 0.8; loot tiers; exposure bands) and exactly one place in the module ever corrects a hand-written judgement with what actually happened: RaidPlanner::blacklisted(), which reads real raid loot back from recorded cases. EconomyUpgrades::rememberedBias() is the capped second, bounded by EXPERIENCE_MAXIMUM_SHARE so it can never outvote the arithmetic. The data to test them already exists (ai_experience_cases, ai_decision_traces.score_components, ai_score_samples, ai_raid_experience_features): replay recorded outcomes per account, measure whether any weight is demonstrably wrong, and report the finding BEFORE changing a value. Deliberately NOT a hosted-classification job - see jev-opportunity-map.md section 4, a model must not enter the decision engine. Deliverable is a measurement plus a reviewed proposal, never an automatic weight update.','2026-09-30 11:02:49'),
 (365,'REV-9','Strategy workstream drained — ordered gate for the hosted-classification family','review','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Owner direction 30 September 2026: the hosted-classification work waits until the harness has completely finished the strategy workstream. Close this task when the mining queue holds no ready strategy task and its plan/implement lane is empty (the WIK/FOR/TP/GF/RV families plus anything promoted from plan/research/ogame/proposals into the impl lane), and note the drain in this row so the reason JEV-1 starts is recorded rather than assumed. Every JEV task and IMPL-65 depends on this, so they cannot be offered while strategy work remains. Closing it is an observation, not a build: do not add a scheduler or a watcher for it. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (366,'QUAL-5','Delete or wire the classes the unreachable gate still flags','impl','todo','P1','W7-3',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/GAP-REGISTER.md, plan/details/research/repos/half-wired-play-loops.md','app/Domain/Decision/WaveFarmPlanner.php, app/Domain/Decision/PillageCap.php, app/Domain/Attack/DailyAttackBudget.php, app/Support/SpaceDockRepair.php, app/Domain/Defense/AntiBallisticMissile.php, app/Actions/RecommendAntiBallisticMissiles.php, app/Ai/Defense/InterplanetaryMissile.php, app/Ai/Defense/FodderHeavyDefenseDoctrine.php','The gate QUAL-4 added already reports these: the WIK-091 attempt log says outright that these files are not called by any runtime code, so no account can ever execute them, naming app/Domain/Decision/WaveFarmPlanner.php. DailyAttackBudget lost its only caller when AttackPlanner was deleted in e23db11. Decide per class — wire it into a real consumer or delete it (gate 2: a slice deletes what it makes dead) — and leave the gate green afterwards. Cross-reference DEF-33 for the attack cap the orphan stated. | WIDENED 30 Sep 2026 after the aspect audits (coverage matrix sections 3 and 4): the same shape also holds for app/Support/SpaceDockRepair.php, app/Domain/Defense/AntiBallisticMissile.php, app/Actions/RecommendAntiBallisticMissiles.php, app/Ai/Defense/InterplanetaryMissile.php, app/Ai/Defense/FodderHeavyDefenseDoctrine.php and the shield-bounce evaluation class - each referenced only by its own test. Run the unreachable-file gate over the whole tree and work its list instead of this hand-copied one, so the set cannot drift again. Two families are NOT this task''s to delete: the ABM/IPM defensive branch belongs to WIK-020/WIK-025/WIK-026, and the offensive missile/moon-destruction/ACS branches are decided by DISC-14; delete here only what is genuinely dead and unowned. Re-check the files first - app/Ai/** was being deleted under a concurrent writer while the audit ran. | RE-GRADED P1 1 Oct 2026: shrink before grow: unwired classes read as delivered behaviour.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (367,'ATK-001','Raids never fly: the target-class ladder cannot open in a universe with no inactive players','impl','todo','P0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php','Measured 30 Sep 2026: no attack mission since 28 Sep (grand) / 18 Sep (pve), 0 raids in 24h on both cohorts. Cause found: RaidPlanner::targetEligible (RV-011) allows inactives in every phase, shipless active targets from Mid, and anything at all only at astrophysics 23 — no AI account is ever inactive and the cohort''s best astrophysics is 21, so nothing is ever eligible. Decision needed before code: either the ladder has a rung a mid-phase account in an AI-only universe can actually reach (a defended but profitable neighbour), or the module states that such a universe offers no lawful farm and fleeters fleet-crash instead. Do NOT hardcode a phase or a target class: the class stays the host''s answer. Proof: a cohort read shows attack missions on the account''s own fleet history.

DECIDED 30 Sep 2026 (judge): the ladder gains no hardcoded class (Gate 1 keeps the object universe host-read) -- a Mid-phase account may raid an active neighbour when the raid is profitable after the fleet-loss estimate, because that is what a fleeter does in a universe of actives. When nothing is profitable the account fleet-crashes instead. State the tolerance in the doctrine doc, not in code. Overrule by editing this line.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (368,'SOC-001','Social cognition is dormant live: no exchange, reply or buddy request in days','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Actions/EvaluateAiSocialExchangeAction.php','Measured 30 Sep 2026: ai_social_exchanges 0 in 24h on both cohorts (389 grand / 191 pve lifetime), ai_conversation_replies newest 21 Sep, 0 buddy requests, 0 AI chat messages, grand''s ai_relationships updated once in 7 days. The lane is observation-triggered and nothing arrives, so it reads as health while nothing happens. Slice: make initiation real against the seeded cohort (DEF-018 owns the behaviour) and make the cohort read name dormancy instead of silence. Proof: exchanges and relationship updates appear in a 24h cohort window.','2026-09-30 13:24:23'),
 (369,'ALLY-001','Alliance lane is static: no application, review or welcome has run in a week','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Actions/ReviewAiAllianceApplicationsAction.php','Measured 30 Sep 2026: 0 alliance applications in 7 days on grand, 0 buddy requests, one alliance holding 15 of 20 AI accounts (75%, invariant ALLIANCE_SHARE). Membership was decided once at seeding and never moved. DEF-002 owns the fit rule; this row owns the lane being exercised at all. Proof: a cohort read shows an application created AND decided, and the alliance share below the invariant threshold.','2026-09-30 13:24:23'),
 (370,'FLEET-001','Fleet saving has never run: one in the cohort''s lifetime, so the save path is unproven','impl','todo','P0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md',NULL,'Measured 30 Sep 2026: ai_work_items kind 6 (FleetSave) = 1 row lifetime on grand and 0 on pve, across ~1M completed work items. No recall either (kind 9: 33 intents in 24h, 0 executed), and ai_phalanx_scans is empty. The save is triggered by an inbound hostile fleet; nothing ever attacks the cohorts, so the trigger never fires and the behaviour is unexercised — including the failure branch the doctrine requires (''a fleet save that can also fail''). Decision needed: either the canary/cohort drives a real inbound attack (the provocation harness exists) or the save is exercised by a seeded hostile mission. Proof: a cohort read shows fleet saves executed and a recall completed.

ASSIGNMENT 30 Sep 2026 (judge): this is a run, not a code change -- the save path is unexercised, not broken (the trigger is an inbound hostile fleet and nothing attacks the cohorts). file_ref cleared so the harness skips it; drive a real inbound at a cohort account with scripts/provoke-ai.php and read the save back. Rule: play-coverage.md, `file_ref` is an assignment.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (371,'FLEET-002','No account owns a recycler, so debris from every lost fleet stays in space','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Actions/QueueAiRecycleAction.php','Measured 30 Sep 2026: sum(recycler) = 0 on both cohorts, 0 debris fields collected. Recycle intents are decided (kind 12: 6 in 24h on grand) and cannot succeed — the fleet that would collect has never been built, because the unit planner''s roles (U1 escort, U3 defence) have no recycler role and the expedition battles that create the debris are the only source of it. Proof: a cohort read shows recyclers owned and a debris field reduced after a recycle mission.','2026-09-30 13:25:52'),
 (372,'IMPL-66','Raise the growth ceilings, not just the unlocks','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php','Research is only ever chosen to unlock something: the cheapest unproducible ambition, a mission''s getRequiredResearch(), or a fleet-slot ceiling when getFleetSlotsMax() minus getFleetSlotsInUse() is zero. Nothing raises Astrophysics past the mission minimum, so getMaxPlanetAmount() and getExpeditionSlotsMax() never grow and the colony and expedition planners hard-stop (QueueableColonyPlanner line 61, QueueableExpeditionPlanner line 57) - the account sits at one extra planet and one expedition slot for weeks, which is the clearest growth tell in the coverage matrix section 5. Also absent: any energy, plasma or drive research a player does for its own sake. Add a research doctrine whose object is a ceiling, in the same shape as the facility chain (host-read ambitions, host prices, smallest step first), and prove it with a reachability test rather than a trace. | SHAPE (30 Sep 2026, after attempts were restored): attempt 1 wrote 5 files with 4 refused - the change belongs in the EXISTING choosers (FacilityChain / EconomyUpgrades::researchDump), not in a new planner class. Wire the ceiling object into the chain the facility planner already walks, and name the level it raises (astrophysics for planet count, then expedition slots) with the host call that reports each ceiling.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (373,'IMPL-67','Read an expedition''s result','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/QueueableExpeditionPlanner.php','The account sends expeditions on a rotation window and nothing ever reads what came back: no observer, reducer or action consumes loot, a black-hole loss or the expedition''s own messages, so the planner''s only feedback is the count of outgoing missions. ExpeditionDurationPolicy is dead too - its DURATION_SECONDS = 3600 is duplicated inline in QueueAiExpeditionAction. Add the inbound half (an observer/reducer over the host''s expedition messages, in the shape of ObserveCommittedFleetMessage), record the outcome, let the planner react (re-dispatch, change hull, stop after repeated losses), and delete the dead policy or make the action use it. Coverage matrix section 4. | SHAPE (30 Sep 2026, after attempts were restored): attempt 1 wrote ExpeditionResultPolicy + ReadExpeditionResultAction and both were restored by the unreachable gate - correct behaviour, wrong shape. There is an inbound half to MODIFY, not to invent: ObserveCommittedFleetMessage already exists, and RecordObservedTransferAction is the reducer shape to copy. Add the reader there, let the planner consume the recorded outcome, and reuse the existing dead ExpeditionDurationPolicy instead of duplicating its constants.','2026-09-30 16:01:26'),
 (374,'IMPL-68','Wire or drop the mine-upgrade-ratio doctrine','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'resources/behavior/mine-upgrade-ratio.yaml','The file exists and nothing in app/ reads it - only tests/Feature/MineUpgradeRatioPolicyTest.php, which parses the file and asserts it against itself. The mine mix is therefore whatever EconomyUpgrades::production() ranks by payback, with no doctrine keeping metal/crystal/deuterium in step, and MinerPolicy carries only scoring weights (Build 1.0, Research 0.7, FleetSave 0.9). Either wire it as a doctrine the production chooser consults (host-read prices, cited sources) or delete it with its test - dead behaviour data is worse than none, because it reads as policy. Coverage matrix section 5; WIK-061 and WIK-183 propose the same doctrine from the corpus. | SHAPE (30 Sep 2026, after attempts were restored): attempt 1 added MineType, PlanMineUpgradeAction, a NEW QueueAiBuilding contract and its own test, and the test failed. QueueAiBuildingAction already exists - do not add a parallel building path or a second contract. Either make the existing production chooser consult the file (host-read prices, cited sources) or delete the file with tests/Feature/MineUpgradeRatioPolicyTest.php. Two files changed beats seven files added.','2026-09-30 16:01:26'),
 (375,'IMPL-69','React to a planet that has stopped growing','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Perception/PlayerObservationService.php','RecordAiScoreSamplesAction collects a row per account-hour and nothing plays from it: no planner, scorer or scheduler reads a sample or a score, so growth is an open loop (coverage matrix section 5). Local rules only handle symptoms - full warehouse to spendSurplus, a build exceeding storage to storageForPrice, a deficit to EnergyCapacity and the mine-% planner - and nothing notices that a planet has not grown in N hours; zeroGrowthAccounts exists only for the operator page. Add one bounded detector and one reaction a player would have (the mine mix is wrong, the queue is stuck behind a prerequisite, or the account should spend instead of save) and prove it against a seeded stalled planet.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (376,'IMPL-70','Alliance life is one-way: leave, kick, disband','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/AdvanceAiAllianceLifeAction.php','The host exposes AllianceService::{leaveAlliance, kickMember, disbandAlliance} and no module code calls any of them, so an account can join an alliance, found one and review applications, and can never leave. A believable player leaves a dead alliance, drops an inactive member, or walks away from one that turned hostile, and leaving is what makes an enemy''s membership mean anything. Add the leave path first - the one a persona would use - then decide whether kicking or disbanding has an owner. Package 6 social-life slice. Coverage matrix section 6.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (377,'IMPL-71','Help an ally in game terms, not just in chat','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/QueueAiTransferAction.php','An ally can be observed under attack (AiObservationKind::AllyUnderAttack is written) and still never helped: QueueAiTransferAction refuses any non-owned target with PlanetNotOwned, host AcsDefendMission is unwired, there is no resource gift and no report share. This is the in-game half of alliance membership: without it an alliance is a chat channel and a static trust bump. Depends on DEF-031 for the cross-player push/bashing guard that makes a foreign transfer safe to allow, and on DEF-010 for the consumer of the observation. Coverage matrix section 6.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (378,'DISC-14','Decide the violent specialities: missiles, moon destruction, ACS','discovery','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/COVERAGE-MATRIX.md','Four behaviours have a host API and no module caller: MissileMission, MoonDestructionMission, FleetUnionService (ACS attack) and AcsDefendMission. The plan blocks missiles and moon destruction in PvE through the host''s mode restrictions and DestroyMechanicsUnconfirmedTest pins them in normal play, while RV-013 deferred the moonshot and CRASH-005 stays documentation only. In or out is a decision, not a discovery: for each say which is true - out, and record it as excluded so no coverage reader raises it again; deferred with a named trigger; or in, which then needs the executor, the PvE block and the guard. The deliverable is the decision written into the plan, not code. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (379,'DOC-8','Fix the register and task-code drift the coverage audit found','doc','deferred','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'(1) G8 cites DEF-001 for the reaction wake, but in the task DB DEF-001 is ''Ceiling the standing wall'' - the citation resolves to an unrelated row. (2) Wave-6 prose still says W6-1..W6-5 are ''planned, blocked on catalog review'' and ''No row is closed by this pass'' although REV-001 and IMPL-013..IMPL-018 are done. (3) F1/F4/F5/F6 have no gap row: they are deferred only inside a review''s JSON while IMPL-017 reads as covering ''F1-F6 ... done'', so a task-title read over-claims four fleeter behaviours that are not built. (4) No AUTH-*/SP3/AG2 task codes exist, so authenticity work is traceable only through algorithm ids and DEF-020..025. Fix the citations, close or relabel the stale prose, give F1/F4/F5/F6 a row each or reopen IMPL-017, and add the coverage matrix to the entry point. | TARGET FILE (not a code slice, keep file_ref empty so the implement lane does not attempt it): plan/details/GAP-REGISTER.md. | FROZEN 1 Oct 2026 (direction reset, AGENTS.md): no work until the six aspects of play move live on the cohorts. Unfreeze by setting status back to todo.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (380,'QUAL-6','Behaviour data with no reader fails the gate too','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scripts/strategy-pipeline.py','QUAL-4 taught the gate that a class no pre-existing code calls is not a delivery. Behaviour DATA has no such rule, and the aspect audits found the same shape in files: resources/behavior/mine-upgrade-ratio.yaml is read only by its own test (IMPL-68), and several files added in the same period have no reader at all (def-ipm.yaml, defence-fodder-heavy.yaml, marketplace-ratio-documented.yaml). A data file nothing reads reads as policy in review and decides nothing in play. Extend the unreachable-file check to resources/behavior (any extension), report what it finds, and require a reader or a deletion. Re-check at the time: a concurrent writer was adding and wiring some of these while the audit ran, so some rows may already be closed by then (newbie_protection.json was being wired into AiSituationOverview). | RE-GRADED P2 1 Oct 2026: same, for behaviour data nothing reads.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (381,'HARNESS-003','The cohort scheduler misses every cron-minute event, so hourly and ten-minute passes never fire','impl','todo','P0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','docker/entrypoint.sh','Measured 30 Sep 2026 on grand: the last dispatch of ai:record-score-samples AND of both everyTenMinutes passes (ai:advance-alliance-life, ai:reconcile-language-requests) was 2026-09-29 11:50, while every ''*''-minute and sub-minute event kept running. Cause: the scheduler loop is ''schedule:run --verbose; sleep 60'' (docker/entrypoint.sh, scheduler role), so its phase drifts through the minute; an event due at minute 0 or minute 10 is only run if an invocation starts inside that minute, and after each invocation there is a 60s dead window. Consequence: the growth curve was dead for a day on grand and four days on pve, and alliance life stopped advancing. Module-side mitigation landed in e0fa739 (the three idempotent passes now run every minute). This row is the root cause, which lives in the HOST repo: fix the loop (schedule:work, or sleep to the next sub-minute boundary) and note that it needs an image rebuild, not just a restart.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (382,'HARNESS-001','A slice may rewrite a whole file and drop its public API, and nothing catches it','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','scripts/strategy-pipeline.py','Measured 30 Sep 2026: two shared runtime classes were rewritten in place by in-flight slices and left the module broken. BuildAiPilotReportAction lost handle()/scoreFor() and its body became an unrelated crawler calculator, so /admin/ai answered 500 to every tab; QueueAiBuildingAction lost ''implements QueueAiBuilding'' and its constructor, which would have broken every AI build order in the game. Both were repaired from HEAD before the cohorts were reloaded. The slice''s own test passed in both cases. The affected-test gate (9370ec2) now runs the tests that name a touched class, but the writer itself should refuse a file that removes a public method still called elsewhere, or an interface another file type-hints -- the deterministic check, no suite run needed. Also: before reloading the cohorts, diff every modified app file for lost public methods (that is how both were found). | DONE 1 Oct 2026: existing files are edited by SEARCH/REPLACE only, and verify_slice() refuses an edit that drops a public method or interface still used elsewhere (lost_contract, covered by --self-check).','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (383,'CAMPAIGN-001','The campaign lane has never run against live accounts','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md',NULL,'Measured 30 Sep 2026: ai_campaigns is empty on grand and pve, ai_campaign_objectives and the contribution ledger with it. The whole cooperative surface (open, declare, advance, contribution, consultation) is therefore unproven on real accounts, and the rules that hang off it -- contested objective, rank-change signal, campaign brief -- can never fire. Slice: run one campaign on the disposable pve cohort end to end and record what it did; open a second only when the first is read back. Proof: a cohort read shows a campaign Active with objectives, contributions and at least one consultation signal.

Re-scoped 30 Sep 2026: this is an OPERATOR run, not a code slice. The harness was handed it as code (file_ref set) and returned a new test for OpenAiCampaignAction plus an implemented marker, while the actual work -- open a campaign on the disposable pve cohort, declare the objectives, advance it and read back the contributions -- never happened. file_ref is now empty so the harness leaves it alone: a row is attemptable as code only when the work IS code.','2026-09-30 16:41:30'),
 (384,'HARNESS-002','The canary live gate fails half the passes for a reason that is not a defect','impl','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','scripts/canary.sh','Measured 30 Sep 2026: 90 failures against 67 passes in the harness log. The check requires at least one completed session AND one order inside a 10-minute window in a two-account universe at 1000x, whose build queues can legitimately hold multi-hour orders and sit quiet for hours (the canary''s own planet 3 was running a 6.5h metal store, then a 17h crystal store). Each failure also costs a 120s park. Slice: make the window and the threshold follow the universe it is checking -- a longer window, or an assertion on accepted work over the account''s own build window rather than a fixed ten minutes -- so the gate reports a broken module rather than a quiet hour.','2026-09-30 16:08:44'),
 (385,'QUAL-006','The cohorts cancel their own research queue entries, and the cancelled rows carry a cost of zero','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','app/Actions/QueueAiResearchAction.php','Measured 30 Sep 2026: of the newest 300 research rows, pve shows 218 cancelled against 82 completed, grand 85 against 215; the last 20 minutes still show 2-3 cancellations per cohort. The newest cancelled row reads ''cost 0'', so the price is not being stored on the row that is refused, which makes the cancellation hard to explain from the data alone. The host cancels a queued research it will not grant, so the module is queueing something the host then refuses -- the same shape as the shipyard-busy guard that QueueableBuildingPlanner already applies to buildings. Slice: find which queued research the host refuses, and withhold that candidate instead of spending the decision on a refusal. Proof: a 20-minute cohort window with no cancellations.','2026-09-30 19:18:55'),
 (386,'QUAL-7','Delivery must mean wired: 34 of 75 proved slices change nothing an account runs','impl','todo','P1','W7-3',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Measured from the markers and the code on 30 Sep 2026: of the 75 slices marked implemented, 34 list a class no production code calls or a data file no production code names, and 32 deliver a test with no code or data at all. resources/behavior holds 18 files and app/ names 6 of them; all seven doctrine files delivered today (temperature, events, member, reaper, diplomacy, espionage, marketplace-ratio-documented) are named by zero runtime file. A WIK row turns a wiki page into a data file nothing reads, a test computes the policy itself (tests/Feature/TemperaturePolicyTest.php parses temperature.yaml and does the ranking in the test), and the marker records it as delivered. Two causes, both in the harness: (1) unreachable_files() greps for the class name as a plain substring, so app/Support/SolarSystemSlot.php counted app/Domain/Galaxy/SolarSystemSlots.php as its caller (WIK-132) -- use a word boundary (grep -rlw); (2) only app/*.php files are checked, so a resources/behavior file is never asked who reads it (QUAL-6 owns that gate). Repair after the gate lands: for each unread file, wire it into the decision that acts on it and make the test drive that path, or drop the file together with its test -- dead behaviour data reads as policy, which is worse than none. No file_ref: the choice is per file and belongs to an operator or the Plan Executor. | 1 Oct 2026: cause (1) fixed -- unreachable_files() greps whole words. Cause (2) is QUAL-6; the repair is QUAL-5.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (387,'FLEET-003','The reactive fleet save has no inbound-hostile source, so it can never fire','impl','todo','P0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/QueueableFleetSavePlanner.php','Measured 30 Sep 2026 with scripts/cohort-scenario.php on a capacity cohort: it planted a real attack (mission_type 1, 40 light fighters, 15 cruisers, 20 small cargo, planet_id_to = the cohort planet, arrival inside the 420s reaction lead the account itself uses), drove three engine passes in which 11 work items completed and decisions were recorded, and the accounts kept researching and building. Zero fleet-save work items; no decision mentions a threat. The planner''s only inbound picture is $fleetMissions->getActiveFleetMissionsForCurrentPlayer(), which returns the player''s OWN missions, and an inbound hostile is owned by the attacker -- so the reactive save (V6, the doctrine''s ''an inbound hostile forces it'') has nothing to read and the cohort''s one FleetSave work item in a lifetime is the proactive absence save, not a save that ran. Slice: give the planner the host''s real inbound-hostile picture (fleets arriving at own planets with a hostile mission type, still processed = 0) and prove it with the tool: php Modules/AI/scripts/cohort-scenario.php run inbound-attack --confirm must PASS. Reproduce the failure first, so the fix is measured against the same situation. | RE-GRADED P0 1 Oct 2026: reactive fleet save can never fire; it is the code half of FLEET-001.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (388,'HARNESS-004','Run the free cohort scenarios inside the peak park instead of sleeping','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'The loop parks for a peak window and does nothing for up to seven hours a day, while the cohort scenarios cost no provider call at all: scripts/cohort-scenario.php plants a situation, makes the host queues and the module''s due work expire now, drives ai:run-due-work on a synchronous queue and asserts what the account did -- four situations in about ten seconds, measured 30 Sep 2026. That makes the park the cheapest window in the day for verification, and it is the only part of the pipeline that can run there. Patch (apply while the loop is stopped -- a running bash reads its script as it executes, so an in-place edit can corrupt the pass): in scripts/harness-live.sh, inside the peak branch after canary.sh down and before wait-until-offpeak, run ''php Modules/AI/scripts/cohort-scenario.php run all --confirm --cleanup'' and treat a non-zero exit the way QUALITY: FAIL is treated -- raise or update the row it names. No file_ref on purpose: this is an operator change to a script that edits itself if the implement lane so much as touches it. | RE-GRADED P1 1 Oct 2026: the cohort situations are the fast, free test loop; run them in every pass.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (389,'SIM-001','Cohort situations for the dead lanes: inactive neighbour, inbound message, alliance application','impl','todo','P0',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/play-coverage.md','','Raids, social and alliances are dead partly because an AI-only universe never presents the situation a human server does: nobody goes inactive, nobody writes, nobody applies (play-coverage.md). scripts/cohort-scenario.php already plants situations in seconds (inbound-attack, debris-field). Add three: (a) inactive-neighbour -- mark a nearby seeded account inactive the way the host does (last activity older than the host''s inactivity threshold, read from the host, never a module constant), expect a spy then a raid decision; (b) inbound-message -- a host ChatMessage from another player to the account, expect an exchange row and an authored reply; (c) alliance-application -- an application to an AI-led alliance, expect a review decision. Each must fail on today''s code for the reason play-coverage.md gives, then become the proof for ATK-001, SOC-001 and ALLY-001. STRONG LANE: file_ref is empty on purpose, so the unattended writer skips it.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (390,'AUTH-001','Authenticity scorecard per account, read by the cohort verification','impl','todo','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/account-authenticity.md, plan/details/research/player-personas.md','','The goal is accounts a player cannot tell from humans, but the cohort read checks hand-raised invariants. Add to scripts/verify-cohorts.php one row per account of the observable signatures account-authenticity.md names: login/uptime histogram across 24h, reaction latency to a probe or inbound, fleet save success and failure count, points growth versus the server median, repetition of the action sequence (share of the most common 5-gram of work kinds), distinct players contacted in 7 days. Compare each against the persona''s expected band and print AUTHENTICITY: PASS/FAIL per signature, so the quality loop raises rows from it like any other invariant. Read-only, no new table. STRONG LANE: file_ref empty on purpose.','2026-10-01 10:03:35'),
 (391,'LOOP-001','Map every planner onto the player''s day and name the steps nobody plays','discovery','todo','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/details/research/player-personas.md','','An experienced player''s session is a routine: read events and messages, react to inbound, queue builds and research, move resources, spy and raid, save the fleet before going offline, answer people. Write one table in play-coverage.md: each step, the planner or action that does it (app/Domain/Decision/Queueable*Planner, app/Actions), whether a cohort read shows it running, and the task row for each missing step. New rows only for missing steps; new strategy goes into resources/behavior YAML that an existing planner reads, never a new class.','2026-10-01 10:03:35');
